{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pseudo-metric-fibre-scalar-product","title":"lem:pseudo-metric-fibre-scalar-product","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":2583,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#lem:pseudo-metric-fibre-scalar-product","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-field-scalar-products]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:nondegenerate-symmetric-bilinear]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"lem:pseudo-metric-fibre-scalar-product","line":4345,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[The Fibres are Scalar Product Spaces]\n\\label{lem:pseudo-metric-fibre-scalar-product}\n\n\\uses{def:smooth-field-scalar-products, lem:nondegenerate-symmetric-bilinear}\n\n\n\n\nIf $g$ is a smooth field of scalar products on a bundle with finite-dimensional\nfibres, then $(V_b,g_b)$ is a scalar product space for every $b\\in B$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:smooth-field-scalar-products,lem:nondegenerate-symmetric-bilinear}\n\\sketch Symmetry and bilinearity follow from the definition, while its witness\ncondition is equivalent to nondegeneracy by Lemma\n\\ref{lem:nondegenerate-symmetric-bilinear}.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[The Fibres are Scalar Product Spaces] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a70736575646f2d6d65747269632d66696272652d7363616c61722d70726f64756374\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asmooth-field-scalar-products\">↗ def:smooth-field-scalar-products</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anondegenerate-symmetric-bilinear\">↗ lem:nondegenerate-symmetric-bilinear</a> <p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g$\">$g$</span> is a smooth field of scalar products on a bundle with finite-dimensional fibres, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(V_b,g_b)$\">$(V_b,g_b)$</span> is a scalar product space for every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$b\\in B$\">$b\\in B$</span>.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asmooth-field-scalar-products\">↗ def:smooth-field-scalar-products</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anondegenerate-symmetric-bilinear\">↗ lem:nondegenerate-symmetric-bilinear</a> \\sketch Symmetry and bilinearity follow from the definition, while its witness condition is equivalent to nondegeneracy by Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anondegenerate-symmetric-bilinear\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:nondegenerate-symmetric-bilinear\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6e6f6e646567656e65726174652d73796d6d65747269632d62696c696e656172\">16</a>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-field-scalar-products","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pseudo-metric-pairing-smooth","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-field-scalar-products","title":"def:smooth-field-scalar-produc